    metaDescription: "Florida Statute 794.011 grades sexual battery by the age of each person and by whether force is alleged, from a third degree felony to a capital felony.",
    lead: "Sexual battery is defined in Florida Statute 794.011(1)(j) as oral, anal, or female genital penetration by, or union with, the sexual organ of another or the anal or female genital penetration of another by any other object; the same sentence adds that sexual battery does not include an act done for a bona fide medical purpose. Which subsection of that section is charged, and the degree that follows from it, turn on the age of the person charged, the age of the person named in the charge, and whether force is alleged.",
